<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><rdf:RDF xmlns:cc="http://creativecommons.org/ns#" xmlns:dct="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" xmlns:adms="http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#" xmlns:foaf="http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/" xmlns:odrl="http://www.w3.org/ns/odrl/2/" xmlns:owl="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#" xmlns:dcat="http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#" xmlns:lcon="http://www.w3.org/ns/locn#" xmlns:sioc="http://rdfs.org/sioc/ns#" xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" xmlns:rdfs="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xmlns:prov="http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#" xmlns:skos="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xmlns:schema="http://schema.org/" xmlns:v="http://www.w3.org/2006/vcard/ns#" xmlns:vann="http://purl.org/vocab/vann/" xmlns:voaf="http://purl.org/vocommons/voaf#" xmlns:wdrs="http://www.w3.org/2007/05/powder-s#" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#" xmlns:spdx="http://spdx.org/rdf/terms#" xmlns:time="http://www.w3.org/2006/time#" xmlns:dcatap="http://data.europa.eu/r5r/" xmlns:stat="http://data.europa.eu/s1n/statdcat-ap/" xmlns:qb="http://purl.org/linked-data/cube#" ><dcat:Dataset rdf:about="http://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/web/products-datasets/-/sdg_09_70"><dct:issued rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2021-06-07</dct:issued><dcat:keyword  xml:lang="de">Luftschadstoffe und Treibhausgasemissionen</dcat:keyword><dcat:keyword  xml:lang="en">Air pollutants and greenhouse gases</dcat:keyword><dcat:keyword  xml:lang="fr">Polluants atmosphériques et gaz à effet de serre</dcat:keyword><dcat:keyword  xml:lang="de">Zeitliche Frequenz</dcat:keyword><dcat:keyword  xml:lang="en">Time frequency</dcat:keyword><dcat:keyword  xml:lang="fr">Fréquence (relative au temps)</dcat:keyword><dcat:keyword  xml:lang="de">Geopolitische Meldeeinheit</dcat:keyword><dcat:keyword  xml:lang="en">Geopolitical entity (reporting)</dcat:keyword><dcat:keyword  xml:lang="fr">Entité géopolitique (déclarante)</dcat:keyword><dcat:keyword  xml:lang="de">Statistische Systematik der Wirtschaftszweige in der Europäischen Gemeinschaft (NACE Rev. 2)</dcat:keyword><dcat:keyword  xml:lang="en">Statistical classification of economic activities in the European Community (NACE Rev. 2)</dcat:keyword><dcat:keyword  xml:lang="fr">Nomenclature statistique des activités économiques dans la Communauté européenne (NACE Rév. 2)</dcat:keyword><dcat:keyword  xml:lang="de">Volkswirtschaftliche Gesamtrechnungen Indikator (ESVG 2010)</dcat:keyword><dcat:keyword  xml:lang="en">National accounts indicator (ESA 2010)</dcat:keyword><dcat:keyword  xml:lang="fr">Indicateur des comptes nationaux (SEC 2010)</dcat:keyword><dcat:keyword  xml:lang="de">Maßeinheit</dcat:keyword><dcat:keyword  xml:lang="en">Unit of measure</dcat:keyword><dcat:keyword  xml:lang="fr">Unité de mesure</dcat:keyword><dct:type><skos:Concept  rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/dataset-type/STATISTICAL"/></dct:type><dct:title xml:lang="en">Air emission intensity from industry</dct:title><dct:description xml:lang="en">&lt;p&gt;This indicator measures the emissions intensity of particulate matter (PM10 and PM2.5) from the manufacturing sector (NACE Rev. 2 sector ‘C’). Air emissions are defined as flows of gaseous and particulate materials emitted into the atmosphere. Fine and coarse particulates (PM10) are less than 10 micrometres in diameter and can be carried deep into the lungs, where they can cause inflammation and exacerbate the condition of people suffering from heart and lung diseases. Fine particulates (PM2.5) are less than 2.5 micrometres in diameter and are therefore a subset of the PM10 particles. Their negative health impacts are more serious than PM10 because they can be drawn further into the lungs and may be more toxic. Emission intensity is calculated by dividing the sector’s PM emissions by its gross value added (GVA), which is defined as output (at basic prices) minus intermediate consumption (at purchaser prices).&lt;/p&gt;</dct:description><dct:title xml:lang="fr">Intensité des emissions dans l&apos;air causé par l&apos;industrie</dct:title><dct:description xml:lang="fr">&lt;p&gt;Cet indicateur mesure l’intensité des émissions de particules (PM10 et PM2.5) du secteur manufacturier (secteur C de la NACE Rév. 2). Les émissions atmosphériques sont définies comme les flux de matières gazeuses et particulaires émises dans l’atmosphère. Les particules fines et grossières (PM10) ont un diamètre inférieur à 10 micromètres et peuvent être transportées en profondeur dans les poumons, où elles peuvent provoquer une inflammation et exacerber l’état des personnes souffrant de maladies cardiaques et pulmonaires. Les particules fines (PM2.5) ont un diamètre inférieur à 2,5 micromètres et constituent donc un sous-ensemble des particules de PM10. Leurs effets négatifs sur la santé sont plus graves que les PM10, car ils peuvent être davantage enlevés dans les poumons et plus toxiques. L’intensité des émissions est calculée en divisant les émissions de particules du secteur par sa valeur ajoutée brute (VAB), qui est définie comme la production (aux prix de base) moins la consommation intermédiaire (aux prix d’acquisition).&lt;/p&gt;</dct:description><dct:title xml:lang="de">Durch Industrie verursachte Luftemissionsintensitäten</dct:title><dct:description xml:lang="de">&lt;p&gt;Dieser Indikator misst die Emissionsintensität von Partikeln (PM10 und PM2,5) aus dem verarbeitenden Gewerbe (Sektor C der NACE Rev. 2). Emissionen in die Luft sind definiert als Ströme gasförmiger und luftverunreinigender Stoffe in die Atmosphäre. Fein- und Grobpartikel (PM10) haben einen Durchmesser von weniger als 10 Mikrometer und können tief in die Lunge transportiert werden, wo sie Entzündungen verursachen und den Zustand von Menschen mit Herz- und Lungenerkrankungen verschärfen können. Feinstaub (PM2,5) hat einen Durchmesser von weniger als 2,5 Mikrometer und stellt daher eine Untergruppe der PM10-Partikel dar. Ihre negativen Auswirkungen auf die Gesundheit sind schwerwiegender als PM10, da sie weiter in die Lunge gelangen und toxischer sein können. Die Emissionsintensität wird berechnet, indem die PM-Emissionen des Sektors durch seine Bruttowertschöpfung (BWS) geteilt werden, die als Produktion (zu Herstellungspreisen) minus Vorleistungen (zu Anschaffungspreisen) definiert wird.&lt;/p&gt;</dct:description><dct:identifier>sdg_09_70</dct:identifier><foaf:page rdf:resource="https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/databrowser/product/page/sdg_09_70"/><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/EUR"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/BEL"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/BGR"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/CZE"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/DNK"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/DEU"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/EST"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/IRL"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/GRC"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/ESP"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/FRA"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/HRV"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/ITA"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/CYP"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/LVA"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/LTU"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/LUX"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/HUN"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/MLT"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/NLD"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/AUT"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/POL"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/PRT"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/ROU"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/SVN"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/SVK"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/FIN"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/SWE"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/ISL"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/NOR"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/CHE"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/GBR"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/SRB"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/TUR"/></dct:spatial><stat:dimension> <qb:DimensionProperty rdf:about="https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/api/dissemination/sdmx/2.1/codelist/ESTAT/AIRPOL" > <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="de">Luftschadstoffe und Treibhausgasemissionen</skos:prefLabel><skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Air pollutants and greenhouse gases</skos:prefLabel><skos:prefLabel xml:lang="fr">Polluants atmosphériques et gaz à effet de serre</skos:prefLabel> </qb:DimensionProperty> </stat:dimension><stat:dimension> <qb:DimensionProperty rdf:about="https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/api/dissemination/sdmx/2.1/codelist/ESTAT/FREQ" > <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="de">Zeitliche Frequenz</skos:prefLabel><skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Time frequency</skos:prefLabel><skos:prefLabel xml:lang="fr">Fréquence (relative au temps)</skos:prefLabel> </qb:DimensionProperty> </stat:dimension><stat:dimension> <qb:DimensionProperty rdf:about="https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/api/dissemination/sdmx/2.1/codelist/ESTAT/GEO" > <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="de">Geopolitische Meldeeinheit</skos:prefLabel><skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Geopolitical entity (reporting)</skos:prefLabel><skos:prefLabel xml:lang="fr">Entité géopolitique (déclarante)</skos:prefLabel> </qb:DimensionProperty> </stat:dimension><stat:dimension> <qb:DimensionProperty rdf:about="https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/api/dissemination/sdmx/2.1/codelist/ESTAT/NACE_R2" > <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="de">Statistische Systematik der Wirtschaftszweige in der Europäischen Gemeinschaft (NACE Rev. 2)</skos:prefLabel><skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Statistical classification of economic activities in the European Community (NACE Rev. 2)</sk